  {
   "id": "2026-11-01-1030-post",
   "post_at": "2026-11-01T10:30:00+00:00",
   "type": "post",
   "media": "2026-11-01-1030-post.jpg",
   "caption": "Hoy recordamos contando historias. Inglés: Today, we remember by telling stories.\n\nIn Spain, 1 November is el Día de Todos los Santos, All Saints’ Day. Families take flowers to the cemetery, and bakeries fill with huesos de santo (little marzipan “saints’ bones”) and buñuelos de viento (light, airy fritters).\n\nIn Mexico, el Día de Muertos runs from 1 to 2 November. Families build an ofrenda, an altar with photos, marigolds and the favourite food of the people they miss, and tell their stories out loud.\n\nWhose story would you tell today? Share it below, or tell someone at home.",
   "first_comment": "#diademuertos #todoslossantos #spanishculture #learnspanish #dimemas",
   "source": "Feed posts/14 Sun 1 Nov - 1 November.jpg"
  },
